P user account based on email matching without verifying email ownership. This allows a remote attacker to potentially hijack a victim's account or gain unauthorized access to other accounts, including administrative accounts, by manipulating the IDP-provided email.","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"a flaw was found in the aap gateway. the user auto-link strategy, introduced in aap 2.6, automatically links an external identity provider (idp) identity to an existing aap user account based on email matching without verifying email ownership. this allows a remote attacker to potentially hijack a victim's account or gain unauthorized access to other accounts, including administrative accounts, by manipulating the idp-provided email."},{"subject":"CVE-2026-6266","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2.5 for RHEL 8","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2.5 for rhel 8"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-6266","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2.5 for RHEL 9","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2.5 for rhel 9"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-6266","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2.6 for RHEL 9","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2.6 for rhel 9"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-6266","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform 2.6","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat ansible automation platform 2.6"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-6266","predicate":"rdf:type","object":"Vulnerability","source":"cve","object_type":"enum","object_canonical":"vulnerability"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-6266","predicate":"related-weakness","object":"CWE-305","source":"cve","object_type":"id","object_canonical":"CWE-305"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-6266","predicate":"state","object":"PUBLISHED","source":"cv